<fpage>1444</fpage><lpage>1450</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">2202842</pub-id></element-citation></ref></ref-list></back><floats-group><fig id="F1" orientation="portrait" position="float"><label>Fig. 1</label><caption><p>Schema of explanation that the frequency of diarrhea caused by CPT-11 may be decreased in patients with colectomy. APC = Aminopentane carboxylic acid; CES = carboxylesterase; CYP3A = cytochrome P450 isozyme 3A; NPC = 7-ethyl-10-[4-amino-1-piperidino]-carbonyloxycamptothecin; UGT1A1 = uridine diphosphate glucuronosyltransferase 1A1.</p></caption><graphic xlink:href="crg0001-0174-f01"/></fig></floats-group></article>